      "text": "We are given that $\\frac{-21-\\sqrt{301}}{10}$ is a root of the quadratic equation $5x^2 + 21x + v$. By Vieta's formulas, we know that the sum of the roots of the quadratic equation $ax^2 + bx + c = 0$ is given by $x_1 + x_2 = -\\frac{b}{a}$.\n\nIn this case, we are looking for the value of $v$ and we can use the sum of the roots method. We know one of the roots, $x_1 = \\frac{-21-\\sqrt{301}}{10}$, so we can write the equation:\n\\begin{align*}\nx_1 + x_2 &= -\\frac{21}{5} \\\\\n\\frac{-21-\\sqrt{301}}{10} + x_2 &= -\\frac{21}{5} \\\\\nx_2 &= \\frac{-21-\\sqrt{301}}{10} - \\frac{21}{5} \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\nSimplifying the expression, we get:\n\\begin{align*}\nx_2 &= \\frac{-21-\\sqrt{301}}{10} - \\frac{42}{10} \\\\\nx_2 &= \\frac{-63-\\sqrt{301}}{10} \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\nNow that we have the value of $x_2$ and we know the sum of the roots, we can use another Vieta's formula and solve for $v$:\n\\begin{align*}\nx_1 + x_2 &= -\\frac{21}{5} \\\\\n\\frac{-21-\\sqrt{301}}{10} + \\frac{-63-\\sqrt{301}}{10} &= -\\frac{21}{5} \\\\\n\\frac{-84-2\\sqrt{301}}{10} &= -\\frac{21}{5} \\\\\n-84-2\\sqrt{301} &= -42 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\nFrom the above equation, we get:\n\\begin{align*}\n-2\\sqrt{301} &= 42 \\\\\n\\sqrt{301} &= \\frac{42}{2} \\\\\n\\sqrt{301} &= 21 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\nNow that we found the value of $\\sqrt{301}$, we can plug it back into any of the original expressions from his solution that have $\\sqrt{301}$ in them, such as:\n\\begin{align*}\nv &= 5(21)^2 \\\\\nv &= 5(441) \\\\\nv &= 2205 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\nSo, the value of $v$ is $\\boxed{2205}$.",
